 "notes": {
  "Allen_posteroventral_putamen_L": "Name and position disagree. The mesh is the dorsal arc of the cingulate gyrus over the corpus callosum (centre y 36.8, z 32.0 mm in the source listing), not a basal ganglia nucleus, so it is placed with the anterior cingulate gyrus in prefrontal. The true putamen is Allen_putamen.",
  "Allen_posteroventral_putamen_R": "Name and position disagree. The mesh is the dorsal arc of the cingulate gyrus over the corpus callosum (centre y 36.8, z 32.0 mm in the source listing), not a basal ganglia nucleus, so it is placed with the anterior cingulate gyrus in prefrontal. The true putamen is Allen_putamen.",
  "Allen_frontomarginal_gyrus_L": "Name and position disagree. The mesh lies on the medial base of the anterior temporal lobe, below the amygdala and hippocampal head (centre y -30.5, z 21.2 mm), where entorhinal and parahippocampal cortex lie, so it is placed in memory.",
  "Allen_frontomarginal_gyrus_R": "Name and position disagree. The mesh lies on the medial base of the anterior temporal lobe, below the amygdala and hippocampal head (centre y -30.5, z 21.2 mm), where entorhinal and parahippocampal cortex lie, so it is placed in memory.",
  "Allen_frontal_pole_L": "Name and position disagree. The mesh is a deep strip in the temporo-occipital white matter beside the posterior horn of the lateral ventricle (centre x -33, y -8, z -33 mm), 110 mm behind the front of the brain, so it is not drawn. The front of the brain is covered by the rostral and paracingulate gyri.",
  "Allen_frontal_pole_R": "Name and position disagree. The mesh is a deep strip in the temporo-occipital white matter beside the posterior horn of the lateral ventricle (centre x -33, y -8, z -33 mm), 110 mm behind the front of the brain, so it is not drawn. The front of the brain is covered by the rostral and paracingulate gyri."
 },
